# Rule 1: Lesson page SEO refactor

Apply this checklist **one lesson at a time** when refreshing a page. Do not batch-refactor the whole catalogue unless asked.

Touch these areas together for each page:

## 1. Title
- Clear, specific H1 that matches search intent (not vague blog titles).
- Keep catalogue `title` in `src/lib/content/lessons.ts` in sync with the page H1 / frontmatter.

## 2. URL (slug)
- Prefer short, readable slugs (`/lessons/why-learn-basics`, not long WordPress leftovers).
- If the slug changes: update `lessons.ts`, content folder path, image paths, internal links, and add a **permanent redirect** in `next.config.ts`.

## 3. Copy (summary + body)
- Rewrite summary for the lesson card, meta description, and intro under the H1.
- Body: warm tutorial voice; tight structure; one job per section; meaningful CTAs to the next step.
- Keep facts accurate; modernise outdated framing when needed.

## 4. Headings (SEO structure)
- Use a logical H2/H3 outline; ids must match docs nav / in-page anchors when `layout: "docs"`.
- Headings should be scannable and keyword-honest (what the section actually teaches).

## 5. Images
- Featured cover: descriptive SEO filename, `coverImage` + `coverImageOg` + `coverImageAlt` in `lessons.ts`.
- Page WebP: subject on **transparent** 1200×630 canvas (spot illustration style, like camel / landscape).
- OG JPG: same composition on **white**, 1200×630.
- Inline images: descriptive filenames + useful alt text; drop unused assets.
- Match article column width (`max-w-3xl`); covers should not stretch wider than the title column.

## 6. Overall SEO pass
Before finishing the page, verify together:
- **URL** — short slug + redirect if renamed
- **Copy** — title, summary/description, body tone
- **Headings** — outline + anchors
- **Images** — filenames, alt, WebP + OG, transparent cover treatment

Wire catalogue metadata in `src/lib/content/lessons.ts` and markdown under `content/lessons/<slug>/`. Commit only when the user asks.
